{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>עצרת תהיה לכם.</b> Restrained from work. Another interpretation: <b>עצרת</b> — restrain yourselves from departing; this teaches that it requires an overnight stay. And its midrash in aggadah: because all the festival days they offered sacrifices corresponding to the seventy nations, and now they are about to leave, the Omnipresent said to them in request from you: make Me a small feast so that I may enjoy from you (Sukkah 55)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:12.815291974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}